The sentence has one error: "jazdí na bicykli" should use the instrumental, not "na + locative". Standard Slovak is "jazdí len bicyklom", the same pattern as "jazdiť autobusom / autom" in the reference. The form "na bicykli" is possible only when the idea is "ride on a bicycle" as a physical position, for example "sedí na bicykli", and that is not the sense of means of transport here.

"Nevlastní auto" is fine. "Nevlastniť" takes an accusative object, and the meaning "doesn't own a car" is correct.

{"correct": false, "corrected": "Nevlastní auto, jazdí len bicyklom.", "why": "As a means of transport, jazdiť takes the instrumental without a preposition (jazdí bicyklom), not 'na bicykli'."}
